        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russian warship fires 'warning shots' at UK yacht in Channel Europe Issued on: 16/06/2026 - 22:16 Modified: 16/06/2026 - 22:19 Russia said one of its warships fired warning shots Tuesday at a yacht making a \"dangerous approach\" in the Channel, as the UK said it was investigating the incident. It involved the frigate Admiral Grigorovich and a UK-registered yacht around 20 nautical miles south of the Isle of Wight just outside British waters. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London. Trump 'doesn't share European view about Russian threat', analyst says 16/06/2026 Europe Super powers in the 21st century 'often not able' to defeat smaller powers 16/06/2026 Europe Ukraine: Kyiv's historic cathedral set ablaze in Russian attack 15/06/2026 Europe 'Extremely complex legislation: Can they agree on common rules to manage migration together?\" 12/06/2026 Europe UK watchdog warns online platforms as Belfast riots go viral 10/06/2026 Europe FCAS project failure: 'France, Germany characterised by totally different strategic cultures' 09/06/2026 Europe Pope Leo to bless newly completed Sagrada Familia tower in Barcelona 09/06/2026 Europe Nigeria rescues 360 women and children abducted by Boko Haram 09/06/2026 Europe Germany and France scrap landmark next-generation fighter jet project 09/06/2026 Europe"
